CAT = "ukc2DebtCon"; SEG = "DCN"
Q = [
("Under MCOB 4.8A.7, a mortgage whose main purpose is debt consolidation:",
 "Cannot be sold execution-only", ["Must be a second charge loan", "Needs no affordability check", "Must be for a term under five years"],
 "MCOB 4.8A.7(2) bars execution-only sales where the main purpose is to raise funds for debt consolidation, unless an exception applies."),
("When advising on debt consolidation, MCOB 4.7A.15 requires the adviser to consider:",
 "The cost of a longer repayment period", ["The lender's position in the mortgage market", "The value of the borrower's car", "The creditors' own interest margins"],
 "MCOB 4.7A.15(1) requires account of the costs associated with increasing the period over which a debt is repaid."),
("MCOB 4.7A.15 also asks whether it is appropriate for the customer to:",
 "Secure a previously unsecured loan", ["Take a longer fixed rate", "Remove a joint borrower", "Add a life policy as further security"],
 "MCOB 4.7A.15(2) requires the adviser to consider whether it is appropriate to secure debts that were unsecured."),
("A customer in payment difficulty wants to consolidate debts. MCOB 4.7A.15 says to consider whether they should instead:",
 "Agree an arrangement with creditors", ["Sell the home at auction", "Take a bridging loan", "Stop paying the mortgage for a while"],
 "MCOB 4.7A.15(3) asks whether it would be appropriate to negotiate an arrangement with creditors rather than take a new mortgage."),
("An adviser encourages a customer to borrow a little less so the loan avoids the debt consolidation rules. This may show a breach of:",
 "The customer's best interests rule", ["The binding offer and reflection rule", "The direct debit rule", "The record retention rule"],
 "MCOB 4.7A.16 says misdescribing the purpose, or encouraging the customer to tailor the amount, may tend to show breach of MCOB 2.5A.1."),
("A credit-impaired customer consolidates debts with a first charge loan. Under MCOB 11.6.16 the lender should:",
 "Ensure the debts are actually repaid", ["Leave repayment to the borrower", "Refuse any debt consolidation request", "Lend only on interest-only"],
 "Where affordability depends on the debts being cleared, MCOB 11.6.16(2) requires reasonable steps to make sure they are repaid on completion."),
("MCOB 11.6.17 says a lender can meet the 11.6.16 duty by:",
 "Paying the creditors directly", ["Getting a borrower declaration", "Asking the broker to check", "Lowering the loan to value"],
 "MCOB 11.6.17: the lender may repay the committed expenditure directly to the creditors as a condition of the loan."),
("The main extra risk in moving card debt into a mortgage is that:",
 "The home is at risk if payments fail", ["The card company loses its rights", "The interest rate is always higher", "The mortgage term must be shortened by law"],
 "Unsecured debt becomes secured on the home, so default can lead to repossession, and spreading it over the mortgage term can raise total interest."),
]
